<title>USA: Rhode Island Gov seeks to hold spending flat.</title>
<headline>Rhode Island Gov seeks to hold spending flat.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhode Island Gov. Lincoln Almond on Thursday proposed a $3.704 billion budget for fiscal 1998, a less than one percent increase from last year, according to a spokeswoman.</p>
<p>The planned rise in state funding also was restrained, as it was projected to increase $22.6 million to total $1.783 billion, she added.</p>
